From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 20:23:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: bound the system error recovery retries

venus_sys_error_handler() re-arms itself on every failed recovery:

	if (failed) {
		disable_irq_nosync(core->irq);
		dev_warn_ratelimited(...);
		schedule_delayed_work(&core->work, msecs_to_jiffies(10));
		return;
	}

There is no attempt counter and no backoff, so a failure that cannot
clear retries every 10 ms for as long as the machine is up. Each pass is
not cheap either: pm_runtime_get_sync(), core_deinit(), venus_shutdown(),
hfi_reinit(), venus_boot() and hfi_core_resume(), several of which sit
out their own timeouts before failing.

Seen on msm8998 (Pixel 2 XL) after the decoder firmware asserted during
playback:

  qcom-venus: no valid instance(pkt session_id:dead, pkt:21001)
  qcom-venus: SFR message from FW: ... Err_Fatal - vbuffer.c:569
  qcom-venus: System error has occurred, recovery failed to init HFI

The video GDSC would no longer power on -- genpd_power_on() returning
-ETIMEDOUT out of gdsc_toggle_logic() -- so recovery could never succeed.
The handler then ran for over fifteen minutes, 610 warnings at the rate
the ratelimit allowed while the work itself re-ran every 10 ms, with the
venus IRQ thread taking measurable CPU the whole time. Because the
message is ratelimited, the log makes this look like one retry every
couple of seconds rather than a hot loop.

Count consecutive failures, back off exponentially, and give up after
five attempts. core->sys_error stays set on give-up, which is what every
HFI entry point already tests, so calls fail cleanly rather than hang;
the counter is reset when a new system error arrives and when recovery
succeeds. Recovering the hardware from this state needs a reboot either
way, but the machine should not spin until then.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index 8c273c6b1193..4712652d1aca 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -108,7 +108,8 @@ static void venus_event_notify(struct venus_core *core, u32 event)
 	}
 
 	mutex_lock(&core->lock);
-	set_bit(0, &core->sys_error);
+	if (!test_and_set_bit(0, &core->sys_error))
+		core->sys_error_attempts = 0;
 	set_bit(0, &core->dump_core);
 	list_for_each_entry(inst, &core->instances, list)
 		inst->ops->event_notify(inst, EVT_SESSION_ERROR, NULL);
@@ -123,6 +124,14 @@ static const struct hfi_core_ops venus_core_ops = {
 };
 
 #define RPM_WAIT_FOR_IDLE_MAX_ATTEMPTS 10
+/*
+ * Recovery re-arms itself, so a failure mode that cannot clear -- the video
+ * GDSC refusing to power on after a firmware assert, say -- would otherwise
+ * retry for as long as the machine is up. Give up after this many consecutive
+ * failures and leave core->sys_error set, which makes every HFI entry point
+ * fail cleanly instead of hanging.
+ */
+#define VENUS_MAX_RECOVERY_ATTEMPTS 5
 
 static void venus_sys_error_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 {
@@ -199,14 +208,31 @@ static void venus_sys_error_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(core->dev);
 
 	if (failed) {
+		unsigned long delay_ms;
+
 		disable_irq_nosync(core->irq);
-		dev_warn_ratelimited(core->dev,
-				     "System error has occurred, recovery failed to %s\n",
-				     err_msg);
-		schedule_delayed_work(&core->work, msecs_to_jiffies(10));
+
+		if (++core->sys_error_attempts >= VENUS_MAX_RECOVERY_ATTEMPTS) {
+			dev_err(core->dev,
+				"System error has occurred, recovery failed to %s after %u attempts, giving up\n",
+				err_msg, core->sys_error_attempts);
+			return;
+		}
+
+		/* Back off: a failure that needs hardware to settle is not helped
+		 * by asking again in 10 ms, and a failure that never clears must
+		 * not spin.
+		 */
+		delay_ms = 10UL << (core->sys_error_attempts - 1);
+		dev_warn(core->dev,
+			 "System error has occurred, recovery failed to %s, retrying in %lu ms (%u/%u)\n",
+			 err_msg, delay_ms, core->sys_error_attempts,
+			 VENUS_MAX_RECOVERY_ATTEMPTS);
+		schedule_delayed_work(&core->work, msecs_to_jiffies(delay_ms));
 		return;
 	}
 
+	core->sys_error_attempts = 0;
 	dev_warn(core->dev, "system error has occurred (recovered)\n");
 
 	mutex_lock(&core->lock);
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
index 1fff66db14b3..cc36dd015a98 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.h
@@ -171,6 +171,7 @@ struct venus_format {
  * @error:	an error returned during last HFI sync operations
  * @sys_error:	an error flag that signal system error event
  * @sys_err_done: a waitqueue to wait for system error recovery end
+ * @sys_error_attempts:	consecutive failed recovery attempts
  * @core_ops:	the core operations
  * @pm_ops:	a pointer to pm operations
  * @pm_lock:	a lock for PM operations
@@ -231,6 +232,7 @@ struct venus_core {
 	struct completion done;
 	unsigned int error;
 	unsigned long sys_error;
+	unsigned int sys_error_attempts;
 	wait_queue_head_t sys_err_done;
 	const struct hfi_core_ops *core_ops;
 	const struct venus_pm_ops *pm_ops;
